### 1.2 Evidence frame viewed firsthand
ev/t282-north-south-tiles.jpg (282 s, sha256 8c1b1e4f…c4d2): the FREE-population state — 12 dark teal-grey tiles in two camps under serif headers "South / Pro-slavery" (left) and "North / Anti-slavery" (right); tile AREA varies widely (Pennsylvania, Virginia, Massachusetts, New York largest; Delaware, Georgia smallest); each tile carries a darker state silhouette and a white serif state name; centre label "Free people population (mostly white)" with two teal curved arrows pointing down-left (to North Carolina) and down-right (to New York) — one arrow per camp. NOTE: at this instant the tiles are at their free-population sizes and NO enslaved frame exists yet — the frame act arrives ≈10 s later (census CP at 22000 ms). The digest's "arrows move population between categories" is the film's label-and-arrow device for announcing each counting rule, not a literal tile migration: no tile ever changes camp in the census.

