### 1.4 Variables (§1.3 extraction)
1. Tile set — per tile: label, camp (south/north), centre position, free width/height (area carries free population), enslaved frame thickness (0 for North tiles).
2. Camp headers — title + subtitle text per camp, header positions, title/sub font sizes.
3. Small state — smallFraction (tile scale in SB-A), tinyFraction (fade-in start scale), tile start fill (dark grey) → free fill (teal) colour shift.
4. Centre labels — free label lines ("Free people population" / "(mostly white)"), enslaved label text, label font sizes, arrow paths (two free arrows, one enslaved arrow), arrow colours/widths.
5. Timing — appear start/duration, free-growth start/duration, free-label start/duration, free-label-out start/duration, enslaved start/duration, final hold, total duration.
6. Palette — paper ground, tile grey, tile teal, enslaved rust, ink, label ink, arrow teal, arrow ink, tile-label white.
7. Tile labels — font family, per-tile font rule (scale with tile width, min/max clamps), line wrapping.
8. Easing — per-phase easing names.
9. Phase order — appear < free growth; free label inside the growth window; label-out after growth; enslaved after label-out (validation-enforced).

