**REVISE — T218’s SVG construction fits the technique, but the planned geometry obscures the added-population frames, and the phase validator accepts schedules that break the intended sequence.**

1. **Convergent freeze — inapplicable by construction.** T15’s motion and reusability lenses independently found that unassigned particles stopped during formation. T218 derives every tile and frame from `stateAt(cfg,t)` and has no borrowed elements, residual pool, or velocity to preserve. Its static holds are supported by CP6–CP8 and CP11–CP13. The transferable lesson is to assert what changes and what stays fixed for every tile. P6 and P7 should print the observed base geometry for all tiles, frame thickness for each South tile, and zero frame thickness for each North tile. [T15 scores, Attempt 1 priced gap](../../../../study/recreations/T15-particle-typography/scores.md) · [T218 Plan §§1.3, 2.2–2.3](item-T218-observe-plan.md)

2. **Owner catches — distinct SVG marks give separation in principle, but the defaults can hide frames and the validator leaves a sequencing hole.** At full size, North Carolina’s tile ends at y=209 and South Carolina’s starts at y=203, a 6 px overlap before either frame grows. Pennsylvania and Massachusetts overlap by 23 px vertically and share the same x-center. Revise the tile slots and add a geometry check for fully grown frames and label bounds at default and swapped configurations. For sequencing, the current upper bound accepts `tFreeLabelMs = 7000` with a 1500 ms reveal because 8500 ≤ 6000 + 1500, even though growth ends at 6000. Require finite starts, positive animated durations, `freeStart ≤ labelStart < labelEnd ≤ freeEnd ≤ labelOutStart`, and `labelOutEnd ≤ enslavedStart`. Derive both label groups and their arrows from the same validated schedule. Add negative probes for a late reveal and for overlap, plus a boundary probe where label-out ends exactly as the enslaved act starts. [T218 Plan §§2.1–2.4](item-T218-observe-plan.md) · [INSTRUCTION, Amendment A5](../../INSTRUCTION.md)

3. **Parameterization — the remaining gaps are in presentation and in how the probes bind to configuration.** The variable table covers tile data, text, timings, and palette. It leaves wrapping limits, line spacing, the Delaware halo, and label-out easing unspecified. Bind those behaviors to named settings or explicit derivations. Derive the comparison clamp from `durationMs`; the proposed 21000 ms cap would cut one second from the final hold after the planned +1000 ms timing swap. Derive or check arrow endpoints against the configured target tiles: the free-arrow paths start at x=512 on the default stage while the free label is centered at x=320, and the four-tile swap removes the specimen targets entirely. Record one fixed source-alignment probe alongside each corresponding CONFIG-relative phase probe, including the changed instant after a timing swap. Rename the build-zero assertion so it cannot be confused with source CP0, and record the opacity departure at source CP3, where the census already shows tiny tiles. Print raw and eased progress separately and report the full predicate at each checkpoint. These are the receipt failures already filed for T212 and T210. [T218 Plan §§1.3–1.4, 2.1–2.5](item-T218-observe-plan.md) · [T212 scores, priced cure list](../../../../study/recreations/T212-margin-bar-field/scores.md) · [T210 scores, completion cures](../../../../study/recreations/T210-threshold-grid-map/scores.md)

4. **Bar arithmetic — motion fidelity is a credible predicted minimum.** The closest scored sibling, T210, totals `72 + 90 + 98 + 78 + 88 = 426`, for 85.2 with motion lowest at 72. T212 has no five-lens verdict. T15’s first attempt establishes a fleet warning about reusability at 64 under the older four-lens instrument. At the current five-lens bar, a motion score of 72 would require at least 353 combined points from the other four lenses, or an 88.25 average, with every lens at least 70. Keep motion as the predicted minimum and price readability as a separate floor risk until the phone-width checks measure actual ink bounds and collisions. The current 11.2 px estimate is `20 × 360 / 640`, a scaled font size. [T218 Plan §2.5](item-T218-observe-plan.md) · [T210 scores, five-lens table](../../../../study/recreations/T210-threshold-grid-map/scores.md) · [T212 scores, verdict](../../../../study/recreations/T212-margin-bar-field/scores.md) · [T15 scores, Attempt 1](../../../../study/recreations/T15-particle-typography/scores.md)

5. **Size discipline — the proposed split holds.** Tile growth followed by an outward frame carries the change in counting rule. The map lead-in, state silhouettes, and T219 payoff are explicitly deferred. The geometry and validation revisions fit within that SVG scope. [T218 Plan §§2.2–2.3](item-T218-observe-plan.md) · [INSTRUCTION §8](../../INSTRUCTION.md)

**Limits.** The on-disk Plan and sibling score records support a construction review. Source-frame fidelity and browser readability remain unverified in this review. **CANNOT READ** `T218-north-south-population-tiles/build-record.md` — `No such file or directory`. Build behavior is **NOT ASSESSED**. The saved feed contains the Observe and Plan blocks. I read the named amendments and available score records separately from disk.

